    <!-- Problem 1 -->
    <div class="problem">
        <h2>1. Grade Checker</h2>
        
        <div class="objective">
            <strong>Objective:</strong> Take a score as input and print the grade based on specific ranges using if-elif-else statements.
        </div>

        <div class="code-label">Code:</div>
        <pre>
# Grade Checker Program

score = int(input("Enter your score: "))

if score >= 90:
    print("Grade: A")
elif score >= 80:
    print("Grade: B")
elif score >= 70:
    print("Grade: C")
elif score >= 60:
    print("Grade: D")
else:
    print("Grade: F")</pre>

        <div class="explanation">
            <strong>Explanation:</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>The program takes user input using <code>input()</code>.</li>
                <li>It converts the input string to an integer using <code>int()</code>.</li>
                <li>It uses if-elif-else conditional logic to check the score against the defined ranges and prints the corresponding grade.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="output">
            <div class="output-label">Sample Output:</div>
Enter your score: 85
Grade: B</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Problem 2 -->
    <div class="problem">
        <h2>2. Student Grades Dictionary</h2>
        
        <div class="objective">
            <strong>Objective:</strong> Create a menu-driven program using a dictionary to store student names and grades, allowing the user to add, update, and print grades.
        </div>

        <div class="code-label">Code:</div>
        <pre>
# Student Grades Management

students = {}

while True:
    print("\n1. Add Student")
    print("2. Update Student Grade")
    print("3. Display All Students")
    print("4. Exit")

    choice = input("Enter your choice: ")

    if choice == '1':
        name = input("Enter student name: ")
        grade = input("Enter grade: ")
        students[name] = grade
        print(f"Added {name} with grade {grade}")

    elif choice == '2':
        name = input("Enter student name to update: ")
        if name in students:
            grade = input("Enter new grade: ")
            students[name] = grade
            print(f"Updated {name}'s grade to {grade}")
        else:
            print("Student not found.")

    elif choice == '3':
        print("\nStudent Grades:")
        for name, grade in students.items():
            print(f"{name}: {grade}")

    elif choice == '4':
        break

    else:
        print("Invalid choice!")</pre>

        <div class="explanation">
            <strong>Explanation:</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>Initializes an empty dictionary called <code>students</code> to store the data.</li>
                <li>Uses a <code>while True</code> loop to create a continuous menu-driven interface.</li>
                <li><strong>Add:</strong> Assigns a new key-value pair via <code>students[name] = grade</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Update:</strong> Checks if the student exists using <code>if name in students</code> before updating.</li>
                <li><strong>Display:</strong> Iterates through the dictionary using a for loop and the <code>.items()</code> method.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="output">
            <div class="output-label">Sample Output:</div>
1. Add Student
2. Update Grade
3. Print All Grades
4. Exit
Enter your choice: 1
Enter student name: vaibhav
Enter grade: B
Added vaibhav with grade B</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Problem 3 -->
    <div class="problem">
        <h2>3. Write to a File</h2>
        
        <div class="objective">
            <strong>Objective:</strong> Write a program to create a text file and write content to it.
        </div>

        <div class="code-label">Code:</div>
        <pre>
# Write to File Program

file = open("example.txt", "w")  # open in write mode
file.write("Hello, this is a test file.\nThis is the second line.")
file.close()

print("Data written to example.txt")</pre>

        <div class="explanation">
            <strong>Explanation:</strong>
            <ul>
                <li><code>open("example.txt", "w")</code>: Opens (or creates) the file in write mode (w).</li>
                <li><code>file.write()</code>: Inserts the specified string content into the text file. The \n character is used to create a new line.</li>
                <li><code>file.close()</code>: Closes the file, ensuring the changes are saved properly and system resources are freed.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="output">
            <div class="output-label">Sample Output:</div>
Data written to example.txt</div>
    </div>

